  "scope_note": "Actual existing Windows browser uses a 601-second 16x16 H.264 video at 24 fps and a sparse silent 605-second WAV at native 30 fps. Full-source absolute seeks, initial windows, exact last-frame start and next-window continuation, paused comparison and 600-second seeks are checked against native job descriptors and byte-range responses. All served Source windows are at most 60 seconds and below 1 MiB. Preparations and playback release are serialized; ended shorter local video tails remain held instead of native play rewinding them to zero. Regression coverage includes longer/shorter native durations, rational frame mapping, delayed events, cancellation and stopped/replaced contexts. CPU-only bounded halo2 instance; no browser installation, GPU, programme render, export or project/history mutation. Full-resolution throughput, sustained long playback, physical audio, selected-stream audition and programme/desktop parity remain separate qualification.",
